{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1067617-legacy-of-summoning-the-supernal-entities","id":1067617,"title":"Legacy of summoning the Supernal Entities","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-03-24T08:48:03-07:00","id":1067617,"title":"Legacy of summoning the Supernal Entities","content":"Is there a legacy, focused on summoning the Supernal Entities for learning wisdom and secrets of the world from them? I can't find one existing: Bene Ashmedai and Thrice-Great are focused on spirit summoning, and Choir of Hashmallim is more about fighting the Abyss.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T09:23:06-07:00","id":1067635,"title":"","content":"Choir of Hashmallim was the closest I can think of, in 1st edition the notion of Supernal Summoning was limited to a single sourcebook, and (oddly) none of the legacies in Summoners quite focused on it. Its definitely fertile ground for new legacies in 2nd edition, or perhaps revamped versions of older ones like the Thrice-Great.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T09:36:27-07:00","id":1067647,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Choir of Hashmallim was the closest. <br /> <br /> A summoning of a Supernal entity isn't even a spell anymore so I don't know how it would work, but probably Attainments for creating or finding sacred places and empowering them to make the summoning go more smoothly and quickly. Or maybe they'd ramp up the effects of going over your safe limit when using FMS to catch the attention of Supernal entities more easily, and to safely interact with them where they are in the Supernal World rather than bringing them over to the Fallen. Or maybe they specialize in Pacting with Supernal entities in a favorable way, getting better deals at lower cost. Or maybe they Pact for something similar to Vassalage and are empowered by their Patrin and their ability to contact it more easily.<br /> <br /> The Legion legacy is probably the best published summoner legacy overall. They have some badass attainments and every body part they replace is a Gilmore with which you could make further Pacts. Theoretically, you could do something similar with a Supernal entity, sacrificing part of yourself to grant them a more permanent place in the Fallen.<br /> <br /> There's a lot of directions you could take.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 03-24-2017, 12:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}